Everything from Part II in one file, in the order the chapters introduce it. Each function is explained in its chapter; the contents on the first page list them all. Part I's functions have [their own file](/blog/collision-detection/all-functions): they share many names with these, so keep the two apart.

## At a glance

Their time and space complexity, with $n$ the number of corners of a polygon, $t$ the number of triangles, and $f$, $e$ and $v$ the face directions, edge directions and corners of each convex shape. Python uses the same names, in snake_case.

| Functions | Time | Space |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Everything for points, spheres, boxes, planes, segments and rays, from `subtract` to `rayBox` | $O(1)$ | $O(1)$ |
| `triangleNormal`, `triangleArea`, `pointInTriangle`, `rayTriangle`, `closestPointOnTriangle`, `sphereTriangleCollide` | $O(1)$ | $O(1)$ |
| `polygonNormal` | $O(n)$ | $O(1)$ |
| `fan` | $O(n)$ | $O(n)$ |
| `earClip` | $O(n^3)$ | $O(n)$ |
| `rayTriangles`, `sphereTrianglesCollide` | $O(t)$ | $O(1)$ |
| `project` | $O(v)$ | $O(v)$ |
| `convexShapesCollide` | $O((f + e^2) \cdot v)$ | $O(f + e^2 + v)$ |
| `axesTurnedAroundY`, `orientedBoxShape`, `orientedBoxesCollide`, `boxToOriented`, `triangleShape`, `triangleBoxCollide` | $O(1)$ | $O(1)$ |

